# Packages a machine keeps at its installed version because an upgrade broke it there
# (station-maintenance beast-arch 76/87). The packages stage passes them to pacman --ignore, so
# they are neither upgraded by a repo-date bump nor downgraded by a rollback.
#   <host> <package> <version that broke> -- <reason>
# ONE package per line: dropping one hold can never take another with it (task 87's hold was
# lost exactly that way, on a shared line). `fleet push` lists every hold with the version the
# new date carries; when that differs from the one that broke, try it and drop the line.
